WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:01.120
Movie

00:01.120 --> 00:06.440
Let's connect the dots. Have you ever wondered what those twinkling lights in the night sky are?

00:07.280 --> 00:12.040
They're stars just like our Sun only much much farther away and

00:12.680 --> 00:19.060
If we connect these stars like a giant cosmic dot-to-dot game, they form patterns we call

00:19.640 --> 00:20.840
constellations

00:20.840 --> 00:25.200
These constellations have been used for centuries to navigate and tell stories

00:25.800 --> 00:29.380
They're like an enormous puzzle stretching across the entire sky

00:30.120 --> 00:34.440
Every star you see is part of this incredible cosmic puzzle

00:35.040 --> 00:39.160
Isn't that something? Do you know how many constellations there are in?

00:39.960 --> 00:47.920
The vast expanse of the night sky there are 88 recognized constellations each with its own unique pattern and story

00:49.000 --> 00:54.360
Some of these constellations are more well known than others take for instance the Big Dipper

00:55.000 --> 00:59.080
It's part of a larger constellation known as Ursa Major or the Great Bear

01:00.080 --> 01:03.180
Legend says it's a celestial bear forever chased by hunters

01:03.560 --> 01:05.560
then we have Orion a

01:05.840 --> 01:08.920
constellation named after a great hunter from Greek mythology if

01:09.520 --> 01:11.920
You gaze at the sky on a clear winter night

01:11.920 --> 01:15.760
You can easily spot it by finding three bright stars close together

01:16.440 --> 01:18.440
forming Orion's belt

01:18.680 --> 01:22.000
These constellations are more than just clusters of stars

01:22.920 --> 01:30.800
They are the universe's way of telling tales of sharing wisdom and of connecting us all under the same starlit canopy

01:31.520 --> 01:37.320
So every time you look up at the sky, you're seeing a part of a grand story written in the stars

01:38.920 --> 01:42.480
Constellations aren't just groups of stars. They're also ancient stories

01:43.480 --> 01:50.000
For centuries different cultures around the world have looked up at the same night sky and painted their own tales in the stars

01:50.880 --> 01:57.480
These celestial narratives have guided sailors marked the change of seasons and inspired countless works of art and mythology

01:58.280 --> 02:04.520
From the heroic Orion to the majestic Ursa Major every constellation has a story to tell

02:05.320 --> 02:12.380
So the next time you look at the stars remember you're not just looking at lights in the sky. You're looking at ancient stories

